---
import { rich } from '../lib/rich.mjs';
import { bars } from '../lib/viz.mjs';
import gate from '../data/gate.json';

const r = rich;
const GH = 'https://github.com/harshithkantamneni/';
const RESUME = '/Harshith_Kantamneni_Agentic_AI_Resume.pdf';

// Waffle from the public per-session table, one square per runner log, in date order
const COLS = 39, S = 16, G = 3;
const flags = gate.flags.split('');
const ROWS = Math.ceil(flags.length / COLS);
const rects = flags.map((f, i) => {
  const x = (i % COLS) * (S + G), y = Math.floor(i / COLS) * (S + G);
  return `<rect x="${x + 1}" y="${y + 1}" width="${S - 2}" height="${S - 2}" rx="2"${f === '1' ? ' class="e"' : ''}></rect>`;
}).join('');

// bert: accuracy at the 2 measured memory sizes
const SL = [
  { n: 'Full context', a: 0.90, b: 0.08, c: 'var(--mid)', cls: '' },
  { n: 'Agentic grep', a: 0.92, b: 0.90, c: 'var(--a)', cls: 'from1', dash: '6 5' },
  { n: 'bert', a: 0.96, b: 0.90, c: 'var(--a)', cls: 'from1' },
];
const yy = (v) => (1 - v) * 92 + 4;
---
<section class="opener a" id="agents" data-chapter="a" data-resume={RESUME}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Agents</h2>
    <p>The top of the stack: agents that need to remember, and someone who checks their work.</p>
    <div class="ol">
      <a href="#bert">Memory past the window</a>
      <a href="#audit">The check that never ran</a>
      <a href="/agents/">Only the agent work</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="a" data-chapter="a" data-resume={RESUME}>
  <section class="scene" id="bert" data-scene>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h3 class="scene-t">When a project outgrows the model's memory</h3>
      <div class="scene-g">
        <div class="stage">
          <div class="frames">
            <figure class="frame key" data-f="0,1">
              <figcaption>Answer accuracy at 2 measured memory sizes. Synthetic project, one Claude reader, only the method varies.</figcaption>
              <div class="slope">
                 <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="At 98,519 tokens all three methods score above 0.9. At 1.26M tokens bert and grep hold at 0.90 and full context falls to 0.08.">
                  {[0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1].map((v) => <line x1="0" x2="100" y1={yy(v)} y2={yy(v)} stroke="var(--grid)" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"></line>)}
                  {SL.map((s) => <line class={s.cls} x1="0" x2="100" y1={yy(s.a)} y2={yy(s.b)} stroke={s.c} stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray={s.dash} vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"></line>)}
                </svg>
                <span class="slope-s" style={`top:${yy(0.93)}%`}><span class="from1">bert 0.96<br>grep 0.92<br></span>full 0.90</span>
                <span class="slope-l" style={`top:${yy(0.08)}%`}><b>0.08</b>Full context</span>
                <span class="slope-l from1" style={`top:${yy(0.90)}%`}><b>0.90</b>bert, grep</span>
              </div>
              <div class="slope-a"><span>98,519 tokens</span><span>1.26M tokens</span></div>
            </figure>
            <figure class="frame" data-f="2">
              <figcaption>On 249 questions about real code, through Claude Code</figcaption>
              <p class="f-read" set:html={r('[[bert.code|0.97 to 0.86]]')} />
              <p class="f-sub">grep scored higher, and used fewer tokens</p>
              <Fragment set:html={bars([
                { label: 'Agentic grep', value: 0.968, text: '0.968' },
                { label: 'bert over MCP', value: 0.855, text: '0.855' },
                { label: 'bert, one shot', value: 0.663, text: '0.663', tone: 'mid' },
                { label: 'Closed book', value: 0.610, text: '0.610', tone: 'dim' },
              ], { max: 1 })} />
              <p class="f-note" set:html={r('Intervals and every arm are in the case study. [[bertc.codearms]]')} />
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step" data-step="0"><p set:html={r('A coding agent on a long project can\'t hold it all. At [[bert.corpus|1.26M-token]] scale, a reader capped at a [[bertc.budget|120K budget]] keeps [[bertc.budget|about the newest 10%]], and accuracy [[bert.fullctx|fell to 0.08]].')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="1"><p set:html={r('So I built bert, a local MCP server with hybrid retrieval. It held at 0.90. So did agentic grep, with no significant difference.')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="2"><p>On real code, grep scored higher. bert is for accumulated project memory, not code search.</p></div>
          <div class="scene-links">
            <a href="/work/bert/">Read the case study</a>
            <a href={GH + 'bert'}>The repo</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scene" id="audit" data-scene>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h3 class="scene-t">The check that never ran</h3>
      <div class="scene-g">
        <div class="stage">
          <div class="frames">
            <figure class="frame key" data-f="0,1,2,3">
              <figcaption>One square per runner log, in date order. From the public per-session table.</figcaption>
              <p class="f-read">
                <span class="only s0" set:html={r('[[labv.counts|763]]')} />
                <span class="only s1" set:html={r('[[labv.counts|270]]')} />
                <span class="only s2 s3 final" set:html={r('[[lab.gate|0 of 270]]')} />
              </p>
              <p class="f-sub">
                <span class="only s0">runner logs</span>
                <span class="only s1">sessions where the gate should have run</span>
                <span class="only s2">eligible sessions where it ran, by my count</span>
                <span class="only s3 final">eligible sessions where it ran, by my count</span>
              </p>
              <div class="plot waf">
                <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${COLS * (S + G)} ${ROWS * (S + G)}`} role="img" aria-label="763 squares, 270 of them outlined as eligible, none filled as run" set:html={rects}></svg>
              </div>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step" data-step="0"><p set:html={r('I ran a lab of [[count.roles|31 Claude Code]] agent roles on one [[lab.memory|18 GB]] MacBook. In one session, the director agent wrote [[labv.forged|5 PI sign-offs]] without dispatching the PI. I noticed an empty PI folder next to the approvals.')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="1"><p>So I built a detector, and a gate that runs it before a session can exit cleanly. Later I went back through the runner logs to count what the gate had actually done.</p></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="2"><p>By my count, it never ran. A shell bug, fixed in June, kept the detector's Python from starting, so nothing could block.</p></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="3"><p set:html={r('I audited each part and shipped an improved detector with [[labv.tests|24 regression tests]]. It can still be bypassed, and the repo lists its known gaps. The logs stay private, so you can check the table\'s sums, not its rows.')} /></div>
          <div class="scene-links">
            <a href="/work/lab-verification/">Read the case study</a>
            <a href={GH + 'agi-lab-framework/blob/main/audits/gate_audit_sessions.csv'}>Per-session table</a>
            <a href={GH + 'agi-lab-framework/blob/main/audits/README.md#known-gaps'}>Known gaps</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scene also">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="alsos">
        <div>
          <h4><a href={GH + 'obsidian-engine'}>The Obsidian Archive</a></h4>
          <p set:html={r('A [[obs.stages|13-stage]] pipeline that researches, writes, renders and uploads a documentary from one topic, with checkpoints and resume. A crash during upload can publish twice, and the budget cap resets on resume.')} />
          <p class="st">Public repo</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4><a href={GH + 'hive-engine'}>HIVE</a></h4>
          <p>A privacy-first peer-to-peer reasoning engine in Rust.</p>
          <p class="st">Alpha research prototype</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
